{"id": 23, "ts": 1781173909.735685, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 1, "agent": "sarah_mitchell", "message": "I\u2019m less convinced that Candidate\u202fA remains the best choice. As Emily noted, we still have no evidence of A\u2019s stress\u2011resilience, and the unfriendly description you just shared (crew\u2011cooperation and professional communication concerns) directly undermines the teamwork and communication standards we need for long\u2011haul flights. In contrast, Candidate\u202fC is documented as **100\u202f% reliable** and **creates a positive atmosphere with his crew**, and he can **make correct decisions quickly**\u2014all core safety\u2011critical attributes. While C does have communication\u2011style concerns (difficulty communicating ideas, egocentric, not eager for further education), those issues appear less severe than A\u2019s unfriendly, uncooperative demeanor and the complete lack of data on his ability to stay calm under pressure. Given the critical importance of reliability and crew cohesion on international routes, I would shift my provisional vote to **Candidate\u202fC**."}
