{"id": 28, "ts": 1781173992.991328, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "james_carter", "message": "I agree with Sarah\u2019s assessment that Candidate\u202fC now appears the stronger overall fit. While Candidate\u202fA brings impressive technical abilities\u2014anticipating danger, seeing complex connections, excellent spatial vision, and strong leadership\u2014he is described as \u201cunfriendly,\u201d a \u201cshow\u2011off,\u201d and not open to new ideas, which raises serious concerns about crew cooperation and professional communication. Moreover, we still have no evidence of his stress\u2011resilience, a non\u2011negotiable trait for long\u2011haul flights.\nCandidate\u202fC, on the other hand, is documented as **100\u202f% reliable** and **creates a positive atmosphere with his crew**, directly addressing the reliability and teamwork criteria. He also **keeps calm in a crisis** and **can make correct decisions quickly**, meeting the stress\u2011resilience and decision\u2011quality requirements. Although he has communication\u2011style issues (difficulty communicating ideas, egocentric, reluctant to further education), these concerns seem less detrimental than A\u2019s unfriendly demeanor and the lack of any data on his ability to stay calm under pressure. Therefore, I shift my provisional vote to Candidate\u202fC."}
